# /etc/zk-bridge/proofs/proofs.env (root, 0640). Read by zk-bridge-proofs-export.service. No secret belongs here.
#
# 1 = after each nightly export, also build the PUBLIC proof tree and add it to the IPFS node (proofs.sh publish).
# Leave it off (0) until the first publication has been made by hand and the owner has reviewed it:
#   /opt/zk-bridge/current/deploy/app-server/proofs.sh publish --dry-run   # builds the tree and prints its path
#   /opt/zk-bridge/current/deploy/app-server/proofs.sh publish             # adds it, logs the CID, prints the gateway form
ZKB_PROOFS_PUBLISH=0
# How many publications stay pinned (older CIDs of ipfs-cids.log are unpinned). Each holds the whole window of beacon
# states and every proof, and the node stores a block once, so 2 cost about one window plus a day.
#ZKB_PROOFS_IPFS_KEEP=2
# The days of beacon states, SQLite snapshots and manifests that the mirror keeps (owner, 2026-11-02: "ok, so lets plan
# to do 30 days of everything"). Proofs and evidence are never deleted. Beacon states cost about 150 MB a day on testnet.
#ZKB_PROOFS_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Where the mirror lives. Another place than the default needs a drop-in that adds it to ReadWritePaths of
# zk-bridge-proofs-export.service.
#ZKB_PROOFS_MIRROR=/var/backups/zk-bridge/proofs/mirror
